  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 AM CDT Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nWarm and generally dry conditions are expected through Monday before \nour next cold front approaches the area. Guidance has gotten into \nbetter agreement that the cold front will move into the area late \nMonday night/early Tuesday morning, bringing with it a medium to \nhigh chance of showers and thunderstorms over the northern Brush \nCountry and Victoria Crossroads. By afternoon/evening, precipitation \nwill move to the Coastal Plains and over the coastal waters as the \nfront swings further southeast. Behind the front, cooler and drier \nair will filter in, leaving us with highs in the 70s and low 80s for \nWednesday.\n\nMinor coastal flooding will continue to be a possibility during \ntimes of high tide through this morning. Guidance finally has tidal \nlevels below 2.0 ft MSL so we will let the Coastal Flood Advisory \nexpire after high tide. We will continue to monitor for tidal levels \nthrough early next week, but they are trending lower.",
